\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Model geometry. The brittle elastic plate (thickness $H$, Young's modulus $E$, Poisson's ratio $\nu $) overlies a Newtonian viscous half-space (viscosity $\eta $). Dike intrusions open the rift by $2\omega $ at intervals $T$; the surface displacement $u(x,t)$ is positive away from the rift axis. The parameter $a = EH/[2\eta (1-\nu ^2)]$ sets the characteristic velocity that couples elastic and viscous deformation.}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{1}{6}{Model geometry. The brittle elastic plate (thickness $H$, Young's modulus $E$, Poisson's ratio $\nu $) overlies a Newtonian viscous half-space (viscosity $\eta $). Dike intrusions open the rift by $2\omega $ at intervals $T$; the surface displacement $u(x,t)$ is positive away from the rift axis. The parameter $a = EH/[2\eta (1-\nu ^2)]$ sets the characteristic velocity that couples elastic and viscous deformation}{figure.1}{}}
