\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Dimensionless CSS velocity and convergence from finite rifting histories. All quantities are normalised by $\omega $ and $T$; distances by $aT$. \textbf  {(a)}~CSS velocity $v_\mathrm  {CSS}\cdot T/\omega $ versus $\hat  {x}=x/(aT)$ at four inter-rifting phases $\hat  {\tau }=\tau /T$. The velocity peak width is locked at $aT$ regardless of phase; all profiles converge to $v_\mathrm  {plate} = \omega /T$ (dotted line) in the far field. \textbf  {(b)}~Velocity at $\hat  {\tau }=0.5$ for $N=1$, 3, and 10 dike events (solid curves) compared with the CSS limit (dashed). The $N=1$ profile does not recover the far-field plate velocity; convergence to the CSS requires $\sim \!10$ cycles.}}{10}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:css_behavior}{{2}{10}{Dimensionless CSS velocity and convergence from finite rifting histories. All quantities are normalised by $\omega $ and $T$; distances by $aT$. \textbf {(a)}~CSS velocity $v_\mathrm {CSS}\cdot T/\omega $ versus $\hat {x}=x/(aT)$ at four inter-rifting phases $\hat {\tau }=\tau /T$. The velocity peak width is locked at $aT$ regardless of phase; all profiles converge to $v_\mathrm {plate} = \omega /T$ (dotted line) in the far field. \textbf {(b)}~Velocity at $\hat {\tau }=0.5$ for $N=1$, 3, and 10 dike events (solid curves) compared with the CSS limit (dashed). The $N=1$ profile does not recover the far-field plate velocity; convergence to the CSS requires $\sim \!10$ cycles}{figure.2}{}}
