\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Rheological trade-off and deformation zone scaling. \textbf  {(a)}~Iso-$a$ contours in the $(H,\,\eta )$ plane for the Krafla (red) and Asal (blue) best-fit values. Shaded bands propagate the Young's modulus range $E \in [20,\,80]$~GPa; filled circles mark viscosity estimates at $H = 10$~km, $E = 40$~GPa. \textbf  {(b)}~CSS deformation half-width $aT$ as a function of recurrence interval $T$. Vertical dashed lines mark estimated recurrence intervals; annotated points give the implied $aT$ values. The horizontal dotted line marks the $\sim 200$~km aperture of typical geodetic networks.}}{26}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rheology_tradeoff}{{7}{26}{Rheological trade-off and deformation zone scaling. \textbf {(a)}~Iso-$a$ contours in the $(H,\,\eta )$ plane for the Krafla (red) and Asal (blue) best-fit values. Shaded bands propagate the Young's modulus range $E \in [20,\,80]$~GPa; filled circles mark viscosity estimates at $H = 10$~km, $E = 40$~GPa. \textbf {(b)}~CSS deformation half-width $aT$ as a function of recurrence interval $T$. Vertical dashed lines mark estimated recurrence intervals; annotated points give the implied $aT$ values. The horizontal dotted line marks the $\sim 200$~km aperture of typical geodetic networks}{figure.7}{}}
